## 4. Local Supervision Interface

### WebSocket-Based Status Board

**Real-Time Monitoring**:
- Active task execution status
- Resource consumption (tokens, API calls)
- Approval queue status
- Performance metrics dashboard
- System health indicators

**Interface Components**:
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ AI CMO OPERATIONS DASHBOARD                                 │
├─────────────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────┤
│ TIER 1 TASKS        │ TIER 2 TASKS        │ SYSTEM METRICS  │
│ (Running/Queued)    │ (Pending Approval)  │                 │
│ ┌─────────────┐     │ ┌─────────────┐     │ Tokens: 124,500 │
│ │ market-res  │     │ │ ad-spend ↑  │     │ API Calls: 842  │
│ │ copy-gen    │     │ │ publish IG  │     │ Errors: 0       │
│ │ seo-audit   │     │ │ email blast │     │ Uptime: 99.8%   │
│ └─────────────┘     │ └─────────────┘     │                 │
├─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────┤
│ APPROVAL QUEUE                                              │
│ [ ] Ad budget increase: $5K → $10K (Meta Ads)               │
│ [ ] Publish new landing page                                │
│ [ ] Email blast to 50K subscribers                          │
│                                                             │
│ [ Approve All ] [ Reject All ] [ Refresh ]                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### CLI-Based Supervision

**Command Interface**:
```
/ai-cmo status           # Show current system state
/ai-cmo queue            # Display task queues
/ai-cmo approve <id>     # Approve specific gated task
/ai-cmo reject <id> <reason>  # Reject with reason
/ai-cmo logs <task-id>   # View task execution logs
/ai-cmo metrics          # Show performance metrics
/ai-cmo strategy         # Display loaded marketing strategy
```

### Notification System

**Real-Time Alerts**:
- Task completion notifications
- Approval requests requiring attention
- System errors or warnings
- Performance threshold breaches
- Resource utilization alerts

**Delivery Channels**:
- Terminal notifications (during active sessions)
- Email summaries (periodic)
- Slack/Discord webhooks (configurable)
- SMS for critical alerts (optional)

